 "name": "rl-p1",
 "purpose": "P1: self-play PPO-lite on design C's plan heads (docs/rl-es-plan.md section 21): zdb's code plays every turn (no per-turn nets); heads 20-27 pick zdb's strategy constants every 50 rounds and on events. Start = plan_start.py (bias-only discretised Gaussian, sigma 0.6, around zdb's bin; Fisher share 0.44-0.70), floor 0, temperature 1. KL leash and anchor gate to that start (zdpp1); zdb (zdpc00) tracked. Event GAE per team-game over plan times (lambda 1 for POSTURE, 0.9 for the rest), rich critic. rl_loop on the box (5 workers, 5/6 of the games), the VM 1/6 through vm_helper.sh (7 workers). Self-play only. From iteration 2: the anchor leash is loosened (collapse_kl 3, max_anchor_kl 5; was 0.3/0.5, sized for per-turn imitation starts; here a uniform plan plays level with zdb, and the known answer CORE 12/8 sits at KL >= 2 from the start) and steps per iteration are raised (batch 1024, lr 0.002: per-iteration KL was 0.002-0.005 against target_kl 0.05).",
